=================== GATE SUMMARY — P2 feature-views/0289 BatteryRangePanel (Windows) ===================
BUILD_EXIT=0  TEST_EXIT=1  FORMAT_EXIT=0  PLACEHOLDER_EXIT=0

Capability: WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK) + .NET 10.0.300 — AVAILABLE (whole solution builds; the app and the
  four BatteryRangePanel surface files compile under the WinUI TFM).

Implementation: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/BatteryRangePanel/
  { BatteryRangePanel.Model.cs, .Source.cs, .ViewModel.cs, .cs }
  Parity port of web/src/features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/BatteryRangePanel.tsx
  (shared state-holder Source + ViewModel + Model + WinUI View). Binds GET /vehicles/{vehicleID}/state
  (Operations.Vehicles.State) via the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine — no HTTP in the view. Renders the web
  composition inside a TsGlassPanel: a 140px TsRadialGauge battery gauge + three MetricCard-style tiles
  (Rated Range, Ideal Range, Charging). useTranslation -> ILocalizer facade; useUnits -> UnitPref/UnitFormatters.

i18n: all six source keys resolve through the P1/S10 catalog (translation.* entries exist):
  common.battery, vehicles.detail.ratedRange, vehicles.detail.idealRange, common.charging,
  common.notCharging, vehicles.detail.fullIn. Empty/retry chrome reuse common.noData / common.retry / common.refresh.

State-of-charge band fidelity: the web gauge tints its arc by batteryColor() (>60 green #10B981, >25 amber
  #F59E0B, else red #EF4444). TsRadialGauge tints from a themed chart role (never arbitrary hex), so the band
  is mirrored onto the gauge role (Battery/Energy) PLUS an explicit state-of-charge indicator beneath the gauge
  whose brush is the exact web token (TsColorSuccess/Warning/Danger = #10B981/#F59E0B/#EF4444). Same convention
  as DrivingCoachSection / VehicleHero.

Tests: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/BatteryRangePanelTests.cs (44 cases):
